Package: hwprivacy-daemon
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         pipewire,
         wireplumber
Description: Hardware privacy daemon
 Background service that manages hardware privacy controls such as
 camera, microphone, and other device toggles via D-Bus.

Package: hwprivacy-lsm
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, adduser
Description: Hardware privacy kernel layer (eBPF LSM)
 Enforces camera policy in the kernel, on the security_file_open LSM hook,
 by denying open() of video4linux device nodes to executables that are not
 on the allowlist. This catches direct V4L2 access, which the PipeWire layer
 cannot observe at all — Firefox and Chrome take the camera that way.
 .
 Runs as a system service, as root, because loading an eBPF program requires
 it. It also gates direct ALSA capture: opens of capture nodes are denied to
 executables that are not allowlisted. That is a backstop, not per-application
 microphone policy — /dev/snd is held by the audio server on everyone's behalf,
 so the kernel sees the server, never the application behind it. Enforcement
 keys on the capture minor and never on the ALSA major, because denying the
 major would deny the audio server itself and with it every microphone.
 .
 Requires a kernel with CONFIG_BPF_LSM=y, CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF=y and 'bpf'
 present in /sys/kernel/security/lsm.

Package: hwprivacy-ctl
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         hwprivacy-daemon
Description: Hardware privacy command-line tool
 Command-line interface for controlling hardware privacy settings
 through the hwprivacy daemon.

Package: hwprivacy-tui
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         hwprivacy-daemon
Description: Hardware privacy terminal UI
 Terminal user interface for controlling hardware privacy settings
 through the hwprivacy daemon.

Package: hwprivacy-gui
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         hwprivacy-daemon,
